config FIBRIL_CAN_NODE_ODOMETRY
	bool
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_FIBRIL_FCAN_ODOMETRY_ENABLED
	select ENCODER
	select IMU
	help
	  Compiled whenever the devicetree names the ground encoders and the
	  gyro under a fibril,fcan-odometry node, which is also what puts the
	  Odometry instance into the schema.

	  The leaf drivers are not selected here: they are on by default once
	  their own devicetree nodes exist, and this function works with any
	  encoder and IMU class device.
